<title>UK: Legal &amp; General firms on Axa, UAP merger.</title>
<headline>Legal &amp; General firms on Axa, UAP merger.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Legal &amp; General rose amid expections the insurance industry will undergo more consolidation in Europe after French insurers Axa and UAP announced their intension to merge, dealers said.</p>
<p>By 1017 GMT, Legal &amp; General shares climbed 10-1/2p to 335-1/2.  </p>
<p>Shares in Sun Life &amp; Provincial Holdings, partly owned by UAP, gained 9p to 247p, while Prudential Corp shares added 7p to 456p.</p>
<p>&quot;Sentiment for the (insurance) group is a bit better now after the merger news,&quot; said one marketmaker.</p>
<p>--Debra Sherman, London newsroom +44 171 542 4026</p>
</text>
